FIND: Two critical data-loss bugs exist in `build_feedback_records`: 1) The `finding_by_id` dictionary comprehension uses a last-wins strategy (`finding_by_id = {f.finding_id: f for f in findings}`), silently overwriting earlier findings with the same ID. 2) Step 1 only iterates over `cell_verdicts.items()`, meaning findings that receive a `final_verdict == "REJECTED"` but have no `cell_verdicts` entry (e.g., rejected by a global rule) are entirely skipped.
FOLLOW: 1) Models whose findings are overwritten will not receive schema feedback, breaking the corrective loop. 2) Findings rejected by global rules will not generate a "RECALCULATE" action, causing models to resubmit flawed findings. Both issues silently drop critical feedback data.
ANALYSE: HARD constraint violation. The operational directive §17 requires models to receive feedback on their findings. Dropping findings silently violates structural integrity and data completeness. CONFIRMED.
